A||N||5||trixterd||V6 replaces the 4 cylinder? hmmm...?||||5||
Z||000000||trixterd||05-03-2001||10:09 AM||||Another newbie question here.  We purchased an 86 Fiero with the lil ol' 4 cylinder in it.  Sure it's a snappy little thing, but is it possible to remove the storage compartment behind the engine and drop in the V6 like GTs?  It sure looks like it would be one heck of a squeeze.  Please let me know what modifications would be required if this is possible.||||reg||5
Z||000001||ChadMan||05-03-2001||10:55 AM||||Oh, boy, are you going to get it from the "Use the search engine" police!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>Everything you want to know about this swap has already been posted on the Forum, but here are the basics.  You won't need to cut the frame at all, but you will need the 2.8 with all belt-driven and electrical accessories including the ECM and wiring harness.  You'll also need to change the fuel pump and the rubber coolant hoses at the engine end.  The 2.8 and 2.5 have the same bolt pattern so you won't need to change your transaxle (if it's good, that is) but the motor mounts are different and will require new holes to be drilled, according to BOILERMAKER who is always right about everything.<P>I haven't done this swap to my 88 Coupe because I'm lazy.  Happy Forum searching and good luck!||||reg||10
Z||000002||ChadMan||05-03-2001||11:01 AM||||Oh, almost forgot.  Go here...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.kickhill.com/mechelec.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.kickhill.com/mechelec.html</A> <P>...and check out the "4-cylinder to V6 conversions" section.  I have heard nothing good or bad about buying mechanicals from Kick Hill, but I bought a driver's seat from him last year and was really happy with it.||||reg||3
Z||000003||Steve Normington||05-03-2001||03:30 PM||||Search the junkyards. One by me had an complete V-6/tranny/driveline cradle already out of the car.<p>[This message has been edited by Steve Normington (edited 05-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||TheFiero64||05-03-2001||03:54 PM||||Welcome to the Forum. I've done the swap in my 88 coupe. The v6 fits in with room to spare. The v6 and 4 cyl cars are the same. It is just the body panels that are different. all the frames are the same thing, except. for 88's because they had an upgraded suspension and cradle. Believe it or not a v8 will also fit without a lot of work or frame cutting. look at <A HREF="http://www.V8archie.com" TARGET=_blank>www.V8archie.com</A> <BR><B>look at this thread for pics of many engines in fieros</B>  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005696.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005696.html</A> <P><BR>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A><p>[This message has been edited by TheFiero64 (edited 05-03-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000005||TheFiero64||05-03-2001||03:57 PM||||My Favorite engine swap is this V8 <B>OH YEAH</B><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PA010007.JPG"> <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
